comments.body:
I am also having the same problem.  I deleted the entire db and started over, which took a lot of time, and if anything it's much slower.  It's not really usable at this point, I can't identify the shows or navigate the gui because the gui just hangs.  It's pretty much been like this for several years on every browser/app/platform I have used it on.  I have analyzed CPU usage, disk I/O and GPU extensively and I'm not seeing any bottlenecks anywhere.  I'm not sure what the problem is but I can't use it the way it is now.  I've eliminated all possible variables I can think of.  I am more than happy to provide any debug information or chrome dev panel performance logs, but I dont think they are going to look much different that what is already here.  I dont know if it's related but after deleting everything and starting over it's been over 3 weeks and the scheduled jobs for generating trickplay images and extracting chapter images are nowhere near completing.  I have hardware acceleration enabled and a massively overpowered server with multiple gpu's, 60 cpu cores and 128GB of memory dedicated to it.

@participant6 I agree that disabling features like this seems tantamount to admitting failure.  

I'm willing to help and provide troubleshooting data.
